   "type": "content",
   "kicker": "Opportunities, Risks & Priorities",
   "title": "Suppliers that combine automation, assured reagent supply and regulatory depth are positioned to capture the incremental USD 2.6 billion",
   "source": "Grand View Research, Blood Bank Serology Market Analysis and Segment Forecast to 2033 (2026)",
   "reference": "Chapter 3, Section 3.2; Chapter 11, p. 302",
   "rows": [
    {
     "h": 2.4,
     "cols": [
      {
       "type": "cards",
       "items": [
        {
         "title": "Opportunity",
         "value": "Plasma fractionation testing",
         "text": "Growing plasma collection requires qualified-donation screening (HBsAg, anti-HIV, anti-HCV) before fractionation."
        },
        {
         "title": "Opportunity",
         "value": "Specialized reagents for complex compatibility",
         "text": "Anti-CD38 therapy interference creates need for DTT-treated cells, soluble CD38 and related reagents."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "cards",
       "items": [
        {
         "title": "Risk",
         "value": "Uneven infrastructure & QA capacity",
         "text": "Resource-limited blood services stay manual or semi-automated; advanced systems concentrate in reference labs.",
         "color": "BDEAFB"
        },
        {
         "title": "Risk",
         "value": "Regulatory fragmentation",
         "text": "Assay classification, validation and marker panels differ by country, multiplying technical files and registrations.",
